# Volatile Fault: "{1}, {T}, Sacrifice this land: Destroy target nonbasic land an opponent controls." Bot2's basic Island and
# Bot1's own nonbasic Tundra are refused; Bot2's Bazaar of Baghdad is destroyed. Then Bot2 may search for a basic land
# (Forest, untapped) and Bot1 creates a Treasure; Bot1 gets no search. Bot1's only other source is the Tundra, so {1} is paid exactly: the pool is empty after.

[Bot1 Deck]
Tundra
Island
Volatile Fault
Island x14
Tundra
Island
Plains

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Bazaar of Baghdad
Island x16
Island
Island
Forest

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Tundra.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Bazaar of Baghdad.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Volatile Fault.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Tundra.Activate(Ability: {W})
! Bot1.Battlefield.Volatile Fault.Activate(Ability: Destroy; Bot2.Battlefield.Island)
! Bot1.Battlefield.Volatile Fault.Activate(Ability: Destroy; Bot1.Battlefield.Tundra)
Bot1.Battlefield.Volatile Fault.Activate(Ability: Destroy; Bot2.Battlefield.Bazaar of Baghdad)
? Bot1.Mana = 
Bot2.Accept
Bot2.Search(Forest)
! Bot1.Accept

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Volatile Fault
Bot1.Battlefield = Tundra; Treasure Token
Bot2.Graveyard = Bazaar of Baghdad
Bot2.Battlefield = Island; Forest
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Tapped = false
